{#- Cookie banner (client 22.10), opt-out: statistics (Metrika, GTM, the site's own events), the visit source and the
    Yandex map run from the first visit and after «Принять»; «Принять только необходимые» turns statistics off (the
    visit source stays for leads), «Отказаться» turns off the visit source too. All three buttons in one row, the two
    refusals outlined. Hidden in the markup: main.js shows it while there is no choice (localStorage
    'dsh:cookie', a year) and again from «Настройки cookie» in the footer. Texts: site.json → cookie. Not a modal: the
    page stays usable, focus is not moved on load; it comes first in <body> (base.html.j2), so Tab and screen readers
    reach it at once. -#}
{%- set ck = site.cookie %}
  <section class="cookie" role="dialog" aria-modal="false" aria-labelledby="cookie-title" aria-describedby="cookie-text" data-cookie hidden>
    <h2 class="cookie__title" id="cookie-title">{{ ck.title|typo }}</h2>
    <p class="cookie__text" id="cookie-text">{{ ck.text|typo }} <a href="{{ site.footer.legal.privacy.url }}#cookie">{{ ck.policy_label|typo }}</a></p>
    <div class="cookie__btns">
      <button class="btn cookie__accept" type="button" data-cookie-choice="all">{{ ck.accept }}</button>
      <button class="btn btn--white" type="button" data-cookie-choice="necessary">{{ ck.necessary }}</button>
      <button class="btn btn--white" type="button" data-cookie-choice="declined">{{ ck.decline }}</button>
    </div>
  </section>
